  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6901.12 Operator",
  "priorExpiration": "2021-12-29",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6901.12 “Operator” means a person responsible for safety and who controls, initiates, or otherwise creates pyrotechnic effects, special effects, or flame effects. Such person is also responsible for the proper storage, loading, handling, use, mixing, device wiring, testing, discharging, firing, and rendering safe of any pyrotechnic effect, special effect, flame effect, device, or equipment, as well as setting up and removing pyrotechnic or flame effect materials and devices after a performance.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 6900) #10067, eff 12-29-11, EXPIRED: 12-29-21\n\nNew. #13426, eff 8-3-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6900.html"
